From d69433b520181553f1cadf64f31e4bdfdf6a1031 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 18:01:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 13/26] phy: rockchip: inno-csidphy: pick lane pair from the
 active sensor

On the split-capable RK3568 D-PHY two sensors can share the PHY and the single
CSI-2 receiver on different lane pairs, switched at runtime. The receiver
configures the PHY with the active sensor's lane count, so derive the lane pair
from it in power_on (one lane -> upper pair, two lanes -> lower pair) instead of
relying on the static of_xlate() cell, which cannot follow a runtime switch.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
---
 drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-inno-csidphy.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-inno-csidphy.c b/drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-inno-csidphy.c
index e2a49f0e2e42..ab784dfb0920 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-inno-csidphy.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-inno-csidphy.c
@@ -271,6 +271,18 @@ static int rockchip_inno_csidphy_power_on(struct phy *phy)
 	u32 val;
 	int ret, i;
 
+	/*
+	 * When two sensors share this D-PHY and the one CSI-2 receiver on
+	 * different lane pairs (e.g. the front and rear cameras of the PineTab2,
+	 * one lane on the upper pair, two lanes on the lower pair), the receiver
+	 * selects the active sensor at stream-on and configures the PHY with its
+	 * lane count. On the split-capable variant, derive the lane pair from
+	 * that count - one lane -> upper pair, two lanes -> lower pair - so the
+	 * routing follows the active sensor rather than a static of_xlate() cell.
+	 */
+	if (drv_data->grf_regs[GRF_DPHY_CSIPHY_DATALANE1_EN].valid)
+		priv->lane_offset = (priv->config.lanes == 1) ? 2 : 0;
+
 	ret = clk_enable(priv->pclk);
 	if (ret < 0)
 		return ret;
